{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "Search for vulnerabilities in public Ruby Gems", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/249343e3839419930f8121f792a11e178e7ceda7fbb904ce14495c1ea85ada45.mp3"}, {"text": "Open-source packages are an amazing, but also a scary gift.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5c479a242da3d2dbc3c05ba8d542754f087f4f33fc7f8b06256742a8a4a26d7d.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.52, 0.94], [2, 0.94, 1.18], [3, 1.18, 1.26], [4, 1.26, 1.66], [5, 1.66, 2.02], [6, 2.02, 2.32], [7, 2.32, 2.48], [8, 2.48, 2.84], [9, 2.84, 3.18]]}, {"text": "When you install and execute foreign code, you’re trusting that the proprietors are good citizens that aggressively audit code changes.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/695cb2546e9fe3d7987ae38b0b132b766658a58083ed73913089463b70e3e2c9.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 0.84], [4, 0.84, 1.22], [5, 1.22, 1.56], [6, 1.56, 1.94], [7, 2.46, 2.58], [8, 2.58, 2.92], [9, 2.92, 3.08], [10, 3.08, 3.22], [11, 3.22, 3.8], [12, 3.8, 3.94], [13, 3.94, 4.1], [14, 4.1, 4.5], [15, 4.5, 4.84], [16, 4.84, 5.36], [17, 5.36, 5.76], [18, 5.76, 6.18], [19, 6.18, 6.58]]}, {"text": "On my dev laptop, I have unencrypted bitcoin wallets and API keys hardcoded in environment variables that any program would have access to when run.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d826191fbb59c046699f41490574236e3fa692fc9841f3357192587974a87739.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.56], [3, 0.56, 0.92], [4, 1.26, 1.32], [5, 1.32, 1.52], [6, 1.52, 2.12], [8, 2.46, 3.0], [9, 3.0, 3.18], [10, 3.18, 3.54], [11, 3.54, 3.94], [14, 4.7, 5.1], [15, 5.1, 5.54], [16, 5.54, 5.82], [17, 5.82, 6.04], [18, 6.04, 6.4], [19, 6.4, 6.6], [20, 6.6, 6.74], [21, 6.74, 7.08], [22, 7.08, 7.38], [24, 7.56, 7.8]]}, {"text": "Package hosts make it difficult for devs to audit the hosted code because there is no tight coupling between code-viewing platforms like Github and the compressed code that is hosted on the package tool.", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/742cdd127486d810f6c15f2b6aa5c6c0b6cc1ab6acdcc7f4250c4863b270a6a9.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.5], [1, 0.5, 0.72], [2, 0.72, 1.08], [3, 1.08, 1.22], [4, 1.22, 1.62], [5, 1.62, 1.92], [6, 1.92, 2.32], [7, 2.32, 2.42], [8, 2.42, 2.6], [9, 2.6, 2.8], [10, 2.8, 3.06], [11, 3.06, 3.4], [12, 3.4, 4.02], [13, 4.02, 4.22], [14, 4.22, 4.4], [15, 4.4, 4.6], [16, 4.6, 4.88], [17, 4.88, 5.32], [18, 5.32, 5.72], [20, 6.32, 6.84], [21, 6.84, 7.22], [23, 7.58, 8.2], [24, 8.2, 8.3], [25, 8.3, 8.62], [26, 8.62, 9.04], [27, 9.04, 9.26], [28, 9.26, 9.4], [29, 9.4, 9.7], [30, 9.7, 9.9], [31, 9.9, 10.02], [32, 10.02, 10.3], [33, 10.3, 10.6]]}, {"text": "The code shared on Github could be completely different than the code hosted on the package server since the servers are not connected.", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/de9ffd901a3d5384b9d2560f7b21779e90747729de7a5e8b410bd9b5fd61146c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.7], [3, 0.7, 0.92], [4, 0.92, 1.14], [5, 1.14, 1.52], [6, 1.52, 1.66], [7, 1.66, 2.06], [8, 2.06, 2.42], [9, 2.42, 2.66], [10, 2.66, 2.78], [11, 2.78, 2.94], [12, 2.94, 3.3], [13, 3.3, 3.44], [14, 3.44, 3.54], [15, 3.54, 3.8], [16, 3.8, 4.2], [17, 4.56, 4.76], [18, 4.76, 4.98], [19, 4.98, 5.3], [20, 5.3, 5.58], [21, 5.58, 5.74], [22, 5.74, 6.16]]}, {"text": "The only true way to audit the library you’re using is to fetch, unpack, and inspect the millions of lines yourself.", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/567e17c7fc64ec928b39db7190cd15714e6f907c86632db42eb4ef70e0aab2e8.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.14], [1, 0.14, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 0.86], [4, 0.86, 1.04], [5, 1.04, 1.26], [6, 1.26, 1.46], [7, 1.46, 1.8], [8, 1.8, 2.16], [9, 2.16, 2.48], [10, 2.48, 2.76], [11, 2.76, 2.9], [12, 2.9, 3.18], [13, 3.48, 3.74], [14, 4.22, 4.3], [15, 4.3, 4.7], [16, 4.7, 4.92], [17, 4.92, 5.24], [18, 5.24, 5.52], [19, 5.52, 5.74], [20, 5.74, 6.1]]}, {"text": "Who has time to audit everything?", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ae06107fad467da5085aee59164c7de935ce1c05d3e57b5377cfa784a8654b35.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 0.94], [4, 0.94, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.68]]}, {"text": "Ruby’s monkey patching and bundler tooling leave apps vulnerable to a variety of remote code execution attacks.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/af3348fca3b528921ef7eb140eca7132dbb97a162dc7c5e9db73bb0f36b08fcf.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.42], [1, 0.42, 0.66], [2, 0.66, 1.18], [3, 1.18, 1.4], [4, 1.4, 1.8], [5, 1.8, 2.26], [6, 2.26, 2.58], [7, 2.58, 2.9], [8, 2.9, 3.3], [9, 3.3, 3.8], [10, 3.8, 3.92], [11, 3.92, 4.3], [12, 4.3, 4.58], [13, 4.58, 4.82], [14, 4.82, 5.12], [15, 5.12, 5.7], [16, 5.7, 6.08]]}, {"text": "I downloaded the latest version of every gem hosted on RubyGems.org to find what malware could be lying hidden in the open.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/792b983ba39994189f70ff14bb9706c70bda433a726953943eb7d7013112dbaf.mp3"}, {"text": "I search 2,500,000 ruby files with golang to search for RCE, unexpected network requests, and more.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/95257f2cfd0fae043c0d46ea031b98b6cd567066ab17c3d2b2742b7937b2c62b.mp3"}, {"text": "Malicions extconf.rb", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a1338bbe50aedae07ac81a4b62b2fb04daf20e9b8f617a20d839ee7f4e78115c.mp3"}, {"text": "During the bundle install process, code is executed from the gem if there is a extconf.rb file.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a7c86afde437650c1b9bb29979aed5846ecaa02bd46f65e285df916a64b39061.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 1.0], [4, 1.0, 1.76], [5, 2.12, 2.24], [6, 2.24, 2.42], [7, 2.42, 2.86], [8, 2.86, 3.1], [9, 3.1, 3.22], [10, 3.22, 3.44], [11, 3.44, 3.74], [12, 3.74, 3.9], [13, 3.9, 4.1], [16, 5.22, 5.54]]}, {"text": "extconf.rb by design contains instructions on how to build c libraries when installing the gem.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/146f0b640b5369173b80bcdeb9ef37b7ecb0b7723676c491996700cc01505a96.mp3", "words": [[3, 1.32, 1.76], [4, 1.76, 2.42], [5, 2.42, 2.78], [6, 2.78, 2.94], [7, 2.94, 3.04], [8, 3.04, 3.28], [9, 3.28, 3.6], [11, 4.08, 4.42], [12, 4.42, 4.84], [13, 4.84, 5.04], [14, 5.04, 5.24]]}, {"text": "Some gems are written in a lower-level language to take advantage of the better performance.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3972d50cef0f126d5f775549b3e609f9c904fa1575013c88454de36a4b6a60d0.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.32], [1, 0.32, 0.6], [2, 0.6, 0.92], [3, 0.92, 1.2], [4, 1.2, 1.42], [5, 1.42, 1.52], [7, 2.2, 2.64], [8, 2.64, 2.96], [9, 2.96, 3.16], [10, 3.16, 3.52], [11, 3.52, 3.78], [12, 3.78, 3.9], [13, 3.9, 4.12], [14, 4.12, 4.68]]}, {"text": "An example is the fast_blank wherein c-land, which quickly determines if a string value is blank.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/de173699a3e95ce67cd0d45dac8e8287ce959054221a3acff1c70175abd4f452.mp3"}, {"text": "Monkey Patching Hooks", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/44b6c2fe12dfd68711fb5bba9b93e14151f80e4c1a172706337bdac6fc21acd3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.38], [1, 0.38, 0.92], [2, 0.92, 1.2]]}, {"text": "Monkey patching first-class types like String or Object can both improve the use-ability of these objects as well as expose vulnerabilities.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a3e203270d83a570c4ad4fd70d7923081f0f791080a5dced7db1ff56f5b9ae0c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.84], [3, 1.42, 1.9], [4, 1.9, 2.12], [7, 2.6, 2.94], [8, 2.94, 3.54], [9, 3.54, 3.82], [10, 3.82, 4.22], [11, 4.22, 4.44], [13, 4.9, 5.1], [14, 5.1, 5.28], [15, 5.28, 5.68], [16, 5.68, 6.0], [17, 6.0, 6.18], [18, 6.18, 6.38], [19, 6.38, 6.62], [20, 6.62, 7.1]]}, {"text": "In 2019, someone monkey patched the Rake::Sendfile to add their middleware to rails code that installed a bad version of bootstrap-saas.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ccd33b2ef232f2267d17d4eda65f6a07a990399fddd4ae55d9592768e46e3150.mp3"}, {"text": "This code would allow the attacker to run arbitrary code passed in via the cookie.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/db53caaaefb7aa74fc0ccb21d48e4a85ddc2de02d5544a31fc03fcd860d071a9.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.5], [2, 0.5, 0.68], [3, 0.68, 0.92], [4, 0.92, 1.14], [5, 1.14, 1.5], [6, 1.5, 1.7], [7, 1.7, 1.94], [8, 1.94, 2.36], [9, 2.36, 2.82], [11, 3.16, 3.46], [12, 3.46, 3.66], [13, 3.66, 3.78], [14, 3.78, 4.04]]}, {"text": "The code could share the machine’s configuration variables and database connections.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c18b7c0e5c095141f385ec8af6060c88ff52af2d94bc04d76907e010c263d266.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.52], [3, 0.52, 0.72], [4, 0.72, 0.88], [5, 0.88, 1.38], [6, 1.38, 1.88], [7, 1.88, 2.5], [8, 2.5, 2.78], [9, 2.78, 3.12], [10, 3.12, 3.68]]}, {"text": "grep for sensitive Ruby code", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8d74e04792317abf87a2414c71df9b8a5485265b540824b19f1d496d4f113f3c.mp3", "words": [[2, 0.5, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.4], [4, 1.4, 1.7]]}, {"text": "The eval method executes a string as if it was ruby code (details).", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f558c51a702356b05605b3ea3e45859532d4ea01ab5e743f865bc43e750b8aca.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.76], [3, 0.76, 1.26], [4, 1.26, 1.36], [5, 1.36, 1.66], [6, 1.66, 1.9], [7, 1.9, 2.08], [8, 2.08, 2.18], [9, 2.18, 2.32], [10, 2.32, 2.54], [11, 2.54, 2.92]]}, {"text": "Most gems or rails applications should never use this cmd because it is too easy for abuse.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/eaebb18938a41456dd4d571371a2ca6a2c973d9e34a15491c0f8ea8575fb61f6.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.32], [1, 0.32, 0.8], [3, 0.96, 1.12], [4, 1.12, 1.74], [5, 1.74, 2.12], [6, 2.12, 2.38], [7, 2.38, 2.74], [9, 2.9, 3.44], [10, 3.44, 3.8], [11, 3.8, 3.96], [12, 3.96, 4.1], [13, 4.1, 4.26], [14, 4.26, 4.54], [15, 4.54, 4.78], [16, 4.78, 5.08]]}, {"text": "Allowing a user-submitted string to be evaluated would let any user run code on your production machine and thus grant full access to your internal network.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6c5a744168d8cefbdd517d87c9df7fe0e015de54db901fd80472c927f204f086.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.48], [3, 1.26, 1.56], [4, 1.56, 1.76], [5, 1.76, 1.88], [6, 1.88, 2.48], [7, 2.48, 2.72], [8, 2.72, 2.86], [9, 2.86, 3.18], [10, 3.18, 3.52], [11, 3.52, 3.74], [12, 3.74, 4.04], [13, 4.04, 4.22], [14, 4.22, 4.34], [15, 4.34, 4.72], [16, 4.72, 5.3], [17, 5.3, 5.74], [18, 5.74, 5.94], [19, 5.94, 6.16], [20, 6.16, 6.44], [21, 6.44, 6.88], [22, 6.88, 7.3], [23, 7.3, 7.42], [24, 7.42, 7.78], [25, 7.78, 8.14]]}, {"text": "Scary stuff.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/dc982b9f158af8cceea55e3ad23ea6736dcb194dca17f0646d0cec6802412709.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.42], [1, 0.42, 0.72]]}, {"text": "The send method acts similar to eval but it can be run in an object.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/41a3150527113473456748e289318c5274abb3546c1dc103a29327fe0470db16.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.12], [1, 0.12, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.3], [5, 1.3, 1.5], [6, 1.5, 1.96], [7, 2.14, 2.22], [8, 2.22, 2.32], [9, 2.32, 2.48], [10, 2.48, 2.62], [11, 2.62, 2.88], [12, 2.88, 3.14], [13, 3.14, 3.24], [14, 3.24, 3.58]]}, {"text": "For example, \"kitten\".send(\"capitalize\") would capitalize “Kitten”.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9b520f0ce0ad86b12051a2619f482518b976c58edb92edf55a12cb71d37ab4cb.mp3"}, {"text": "If a user-defined variable is given, instead of a hardcoded string, then potentially arbitrary ruby code could be defined and executed.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d92dacaffaf2fc716e0efa746498e189ed4e488f59e8c5ddda8dadddd87796b8.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.32], [3, 0.9, 1.34], [4, 1.34, 1.64], [5, 1.64, 1.92], [6, 1.92, 2.38], [7, 2.38, 2.54], [8, 2.54, 2.64], [10, 3.08, 3.46], [11, 4.06, 4.32], [12, 4.32, 4.78], [13, 4.78, 5.38], [14, 5.38, 5.7], [15, 5.7, 6.04], [16, 6.04, 6.22], [17, 6.22, 6.38], [18, 6.38, 6.82], [19, 6.82, 7.1], [20, 7.1, 7.62]]}, {"text": "Most gems should never use the send or eval methods.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9870544e732945803fecd9411f19c50792f1a7ad27fe89d61f6030f7ca27cfb4.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.42], [1, 0.42, 0.9], [2, 0.9, 1.36], [3, 1.36, 1.6], [4, 1.6, 1.96], [5, 1.96, 2.12], [7, 2.4, 2.6], [9, 2.88, 3.22]]}, {"text": "Hackers can also open network requests to a server, sending private information about the machine installing the gem or running it.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/be5cd1f381f2779d1b87085a0ad897a96a6cdfaf7f537d00321e3910922d6c9a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.42], [1, 0.42, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 1.1], [4, 1.1, 1.44], [5, 1.44, 1.86], [6, 1.86, 2.2], [7, 2.2, 2.3], [8, 2.3, 2.66], [9, 3.1, 3.26], [10, 3.26, 3.58], [11, 3.58, 4.22], [12, 4.22, 4.46], [13, 4.46, 4.62], [14, 4.62, 4.9], [15, 4.9, 5.38], [16, 5.38, 5.58], [17, 5.58, 5.78], [18, 5.78, 6.08], [19, 6.08, 6.32], [20, 6.32, 6.62]]}, {"text": "In ruby, you should verify that Net class is not being unexpectedly used to call a command and control center.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f9c7e5a2e2cce08cd2c07382f6ea88b5aa8323706b0307f48ecf79cfa1c4296d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.54], [2, 0.84, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.12], [4, 1.12, 1.52], [5, 1.52, 1.8], [8, 2.3, 2.58], [9, 2.58, 2.82], [10, 2.82, 3.1], [11, 3.1, 3.72], [12, 3.72, 4.3], [13, 4.3, 4.48], [14, 4.48, 4.62], [15, 4.62, 4.78], [16, 4.78, 5.04], [17, 5.04, 5.18], [18, 5.18, 5.46], [19, 5.46, 5.84]]}, {"text": "Most gems also should not be accessing the ENV object.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6d7401f61c523fdb224ae9627d747b148f2556d8d838fcbd63fc82673570163b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.32], [2, 0.68, 1.04], [3, 1.04, 1.3], [4, 1.3, 1.46], [5, 1.46, 1.66], [6, 1.66, 2.08], [7, 2.08, 2.34], [8, 2.34, 2.7], [9, 2.7, 3.08]]}, {"text": "Often developers store their private keys as environment variables instead of hardcoding them in code.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5973e971c518fa65115a9b75b5b7b18eb0bced14c5caca3ae3401c07388eaa12.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.9], [2, 0.9, 1.28], [3, 1.28, 1.5], [4, 1.5, 1.82], [5, 1.82, 2.14], [6, 2.14, 2.48], [7, 2.48, 2.9], [8, 2.9, 3.38], [9, 3.38, 3.92], [10, 3.92, 4.1], [12, 4.58, 4.8], [13, 4.8, 4.96], [14, 4.96, 5.22]]}, {"text": "List of objects and methods to check:", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5c0cee5a1af93243681600b858b43a1ac1cbcb0c5273c5d8d9be055b560150e1.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 1.12], [4, 1.12, 1.42], [5, 1.42, 1.72], [6, 1.72, 2.08]]}, {"text": "ENV", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2c11a49fe4d4a068df2f734933277b03b3d17c3e842eefa56ad1a5972a2ce747.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.86]]}, {"text": "eval", "block": 17, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/12d3557749b2d8e443acd484a88d5b0344dd272e8dee76783f7868d061b01c5e.mp3"}, {"text": "send", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fb1d68860d52d32a2d618aa88d0569794b41c9be5bcaf3c3b8c53782fb52a019.mp3"}, {"text": "exec", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2162252d64fdd89262a1d558165c771901f353f0415656471328e33c2eb391c9.mp3"}, {"text": "\\`", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8a515e61cd994f670037c9f7af5b9b9edb5ab21f997bfcf9725761c4c223f19a.mp3"}, {"text": "fork", "block": 21, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ad558107a5757512c46023bd33b31add699a2140108434bc72e2ecad20942f50.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.42]]}, {"text": "spawn", "block": 22, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/67789d65c153e3f0f3c3a7a29e277104e543b181e498c120cd92b63300717a80.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.56]]}, {"text": "syscall", "block": 23, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f37af5c35254ab2883efe22019b1460004cfee43ad37ab1f2e35a4284d6f919d.mp3"}, {"text": "system", "block": 24, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7b1a83756b410cbdd318436db55c8592ab3351306ebf9026504a6425b9d6b487.mp3"}, {"text": "Searching the top 100,000 ruby gems for exploits", "block": 25, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fe9e36735fcf5388e2e079884352697c620bcc74b08b3293a95840f8d6d27670.mp3"}, {"text": "Rubygems.org offers a data dump of all of the gems on rubygems with how much they were downloaded.", "block": 26, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ce5af9ace0ecf6782c654fcb7c79b3a9a3cfdbd287c1d79a6d5ef3059621bd81.mp3", "words": [[1, 1.02, 1.4], [2, 1.4, 1.62], [3, 1.62, 1.76], [4, 1.76, 2.0], [5, 2.0, 2.18], [6, 2.18, 2.38], [7, 2.38, 2.48], [8, 2.48, 2.62], [10, 2.84, 3.14], [11, 3.14, 3.7], [12, 3.7, 3.9], [13, 3.9, 4.06], [14, 4.06, 4.26], [15, 4.26, 4.4], [16, 4.4, 4.52], [17, 4.52, 4.92]]}, {"text": "For the sake of speed and bandwidth limitations, I will only fetch the top 100,000 for analysis.", "block": 26, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d88aef8bc7b8846d13ef83500bdc50f62b764f6e26a59312c6230cdbb5114286.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 0.68], [4, 0.68, 0.92], [5, 0.92, 1.16], [6, 1.16, 1.46], [7, 1.46, 2.08], [8, 2.5, 2.56], [9, 2.56, 2.68], [10, 2.68, 2.98], [11, 2.98, 3.22], [12, 3.22, 3.44], [13, 3.44, 3.68], [15, 4.66, 4.86], [16, 4.86, 5.26]]}, {"text": "I was a bit lazy and used a Gemfile and bundle install -j 8 to fetch the latest version of the 100,000 most popular ruby gems of 2020-11-15.", "block": 27, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5f052bf7e7bb99ea758297d8e8b950ec5579fb7fc0e57e412d74b76d81794268.mp3"}, {"text": "With the raw source code dumped into a local directory, I can use a mix of ruby and grep to search all of the gems for suspicious code.", "block": 28, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7a6138866dec1b8cb7f74346de220cfb7c3014dedc660fc3d6f1a6336b7af8b1.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.94], [4, 0.94, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.4], [6, 1.4, 1.74], [7, 1.74, 1.9], [8, 1.9, 2.1], [9, 2.1, 2.7], [10, 3.16, 3.24], [11, 3.24, 3.36], [12, 3.36, 3.56], [13, 3.56, 3.7], [14, 3.7, 3.94], [15, 3.94, 4.22], [16, 4.22, 4.48], [17, 4.48, 4.84], [18, 4.84, 5.06], [19, 5.06, 5.34], [20, 5.34, 5.58], [21, 5.58, 5.92], [22, 5.92, 6.1], [23, 6.1, 6.18], [24, 6.18, 6.44], [25, 6.44, 6.74], [26, 6.74, 7.1], [27, 7.1, 7.58]]}, {"text": "Unfortunately, I wasn’t able to fully automate the research process.", "block": 28, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c491f82970f47bcb51c229489b46e2f58a09291e58033618d363fdbe58651a6a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.7], [1, 1.04, 1.1], [2, 1.1, 1.4], [3, 1.4, 1.6], [4, 1.6, 1.74], [5, 1.74, 2.04], [6, 2.04, 2.44], [7, 2.44, 2.62], [8, 2.62, 2.94], [9, 2.94, 3.42]]}, {"text": "My script searched for suspicious method calls, flagged the line along with the package name, and then I verified that each suspicious line was a false positive.", "block": 28, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/860ab7fa24b0d8085eb736e8daf215faec14ac28c620789eedb6166b38847157.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.12], [1, 0.12, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.88], [3, 0.88, 1.06], [4, 1.06, 1.42], [5, 1.42, 1.86], [6, 1.86, 2.28], [7, 2.66, 3.0], [8, 3.0, 3.12], [9, 3.12, 3.32], [10, 3.32, 3.6], [11, 3.6, 3.78], [12, 3.78, 3.88], [13, 3.88, 4.14], [14, 4.14, 4.44], [15, 4.88, 5.0], [16, 5.0, 5.1], [17, 5.1, 5.22], [18, 5.22, 5.58], [19, 5.58, 5.82], [20, 5.82, 6.04], [21, 6.04, 6.34], [22, 6.34, 6.82], [23, 6.82, 7.04], [24, 7.04, 7.14], [25, 7.14, 7.36], [26, 7.36, 7.9]]}, {"text": "For example, a ruby gem that adds a CSS framework should never use eval, but they may use it in their test cases.", "block": 28, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ffd79eeff236fa4e47a51a8a1fe88a5068db4c82786bf887dc6c2a07b2bc2d7b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.64], [2, 0.84, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.24], [4, 1.24, 1.46], [5, 1.46, 1.7], [6, 1.7, 1.92], [7, 1.92, 2.1], [8, 2.1, 2.4], [9, 2.4, 2.96], [10, 2.96, 3.24], [11, 3.24, 3.48], [12, 3.48, 3.84], [14, 4.62, 4.72], [15, 4.72, 4.88], [16, 4.88, 5.06], [17, 5.06, 5.38], [18, 5.38, 5.6], [19, 5.6, 5.74], [20, 5.74, 5.86], [21, 5.86, 6.1], [22, 6.1, 6.54]]}, {"text": "In general, it’s never good to use eval, using it in a test case that isn’t run on production should be safe.", "block": 28, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/23d5faf25575cc0117e24948a3e3be4e67fb90bc283dd3485ce3878048b0f096.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.6], [2, 1.12, 1.32], [3, 1.32, 1.52], [4, 1.52, 1.72], [5, 1.72, 1.94], [6, 1.94, 2.14], [8, 2.86, 3.1], [9, 3.1, 3.3], [10, 3.3, 3.38], [11, 3.38, 3.52], [12, 3.52, 3.68], [13, 3.68, 3.96], [14, 3.96, 4.18], [15, 4.18, 4.58], [16, 4.58, 4.7], [17, 4.7, 4.88], [18, 4.88, 5.3], [19, 5.3, 5.68], [20, 5.68, 5.82], [21, 5.82, 6.26]]}, {"text": "The git repo powering this exploration can be found at https://github.com/KevinColemanInc/gem-sec-research.", "block": 29, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b561d80205e11510111d3c217fb068a888d6c65b7c36ffa66e6b8e58d7e3073e.mp3"}, {"text": "Conclusion: What gems are vulnerable?", "block": 30, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9bfa9bb9f872719705ab5ba40558c35f9d843109f137cf062e2409c9d69a2c86.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.56], [1, 0.96, 1.16], [2, 1.16, 1.38], [3, 1.38, 1.58], [4, 1.58, 1.94]]}, {"text": "Highlights!", "block": 31, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0b963a2dc60f2fef7446df8880a661185b5e2d8895448768819422382ed95414.mp3"}, {"text": "Using sensitive ruby code isn’t inherently bad, so I’m not able to understand the intention of 200,000 ruby gems to determine if calling eval is malicious or expected.", "block": 31, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/393e6bb31241f1e170cf5b8f2ea15fc80edda5d97bca8e3d5f9f4925e7a6ccf8.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.74], [2, 0.74, 1.08], [3, 1.08, 1.32], [4, 1.32, 1.66], [5, 1.66, 2.04], [6, 2.04, 2.44], [7, 2.9, 3.16], [8, 3.16, 3.32], [9, 3.32, 3.46], [10, 3.46, 3.72], [11, 3.72, 3.88], [12, 3.88, 4.3], [13, 4.3, 4.5], [14, 4.5, 4.8], [15, 4.8, 5.02], [17, 5.82, 6.16], [18, 6.16, 6.34], [19, 6.34, 6.62], [20, 6.62, 6.96], [21, 6.96, 7.12], [22, 7.12, 7.4], [24, 7.74, 7.9], [25, 7.9, 8.28], [26, 8.28, 8.62], [27, 8.62, 9.06]]}, {"text": "The much lower hanging fruit is what gems attack the server or developers box via extconf.rb.", "block": 31, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fd53124daab6faea971cbef2d8e8eb6a1884c26bab46afb04e3aea10f844aea3.mp3"}, {"text": "My gemsploit gem sends all of the ENV variables up to a server", "block": 31, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a98d0b1d03943e38732c59418bf2f5660c8cef1f6b909912ad0f75c2e92e0c6e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [2, 0.74, 1.06], [3, 1.06, 1.42], [4, 1.42, 1.7], [5, 1.7, 1.82], [6, 1.82, 1.92], [7, 1.92, 2.34], [8, 2.34, 2.78], [9, 2.78, 3.1], [10, 3.1, 3.3], [11, 3.3, 3.4], [12, 3.4, 3.68]]}, {"text": "Top picks", "block": 32, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/98484e3728c823fe1d0869b02f0fbd17e33293cb31121222511cdaa0fae9fd89.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.7]]}, {"text": "lwes_ext", "block": 33, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e8673a72a2051c38f7f4a78e56f8c40ef5778442cb8196ac5d44f47cff794c96.mp3"}, {"text": "lwes_ext, downloaded 69,122 times, when installed, downloads a script from a website and executes it.", "block": 34, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a4dca90e4dee0c8a5e8eef75fd784d7cc553dd68e73baa800e43d457ec2d9586.mp3", "words": [[3, 3.22, 3.96], [4, 3.96, 4.24], [5, 4.24, 4.74], [6, 5.06, 5.34], [7, 5.34, 5.56], [8, 5.56, 5.76], [9, 5.76, 6.02], [10, 6.02, 6.12], [11, 6.12, 6.52], [12, 6.52, 6.78], [13, 6.78, 7.34], [14, 7.34, 7.56]]}, {"text": "The script is no longer available, so it just crashes.", "block": 34, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7aba6e11312414336e99ac2f481c062fa864c27081f0fc2447628703ba3a9cdb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.72], [4, 0.72, 0.96], [5, 0.96, 1.3], [6, 1.64, 1.7], [7, 1.7, 1.82], [8, 1.82, 1.9], [9, 1.9, 2.22]]}, {"text": "Since the project and website aren’t maintained, I worry that a malicious actor could buy the domain if it was allowed to expire and swap in a more nefarious script.", "block": 34, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b8b614397caa6ebacc4d8e7eeef0a8121a4aa6688ab2c7b29e8e46607ebc68a8.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 1.0], [4, 1.0, 1.4], [5, 1.4, 1.8], [6, 1.8, 2.18], [7, 2.72, 2.78], [8, 2.78, 3.0], [9, 3.0, 3.22], [10, 3.22, 3.34], [11, 3.34, 3.64], [12, 3.64, 4.18], [13, 4.18, 4.4], [14, 4.4, 4.58], [15, 4.58, 4.74], [16, 4.74, 5.04], [17, 5.04, 5.36], [18, 5.36, 5.46], [19, 5.46, 5.58], [20, 5.58, 5.82], [21, 5.82, 6.08], [22, 6.08, 6.52], [23, 6.52, 6.74], [24, 6.74, 7.0], [25, 7.0, 7.22], [26, 7.22, 7.3], [27, 7.3, 7.44], [28, 7.44, 7.98], [29, 7.98, 8.3]]}, {"text": "uwsgi", "block": 35, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/91457a8cab4ab4de2aee79834ebece4147f3174b0c47449238a97ee434759a61.mp3"}, {"text": "uwsgi is doing the same as lwes_ext, executing arbitrary code downloaded from the internet.", "block": 36, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b0095ec38a435ad91a7f58e329a065d191a5ca709b790ff0ff8569e22c5481ae.mp3"}, {"text": "The script behind this 404s now, so who knows what it was doing before?", "block": 36, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e0955c1ca8e230a4d79e30c3471fef0043766e6f2c3194d55f0979084a71154d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 1.06], [5, 1.72, 1.9], [6, 2.12, 2.22], [7, 2.22, 2.38], [8, 2.38, 2.58], [9, 2.58, 2.82], [10, 2.82, 2.92], [11, 2.92, 3.0], [12, 3.0, 3.2], [13, 3.2, 3.48]]}, {"text": "httpcookie", "block": 37, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0f996a6dd7bb543728a68bd70ad85c22a4e7154ff2b1fb25c3d90d473637f0a0.mp3"}, {"text": "This failure is intentional.", "block": 38, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/938b9244f53db9ef0373371cc2d36b286b124028657f6532e6906d346a0b4046.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 1.2]]}, {"text": "You probably meant to install and run http-cookie", "block": 38, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f50cbf869b120f98fab3adca1fa771ab6ebbf80bc1e4201055327e4fe53f66dc.mp3"}, {"text": "In httpcookie, a kind-hearted developer trying to prevent people from falling pre to typosquatting created a gem called httpcookie that all it does is fail on install.", "block": 39, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/47a7f171727806b29dbb0852855dee9b493e9d3c7a709ccbe61bb5f1aea5b962.mp3"}, {"text": "It warns the developer they mistyped the gem name and they need to go install the correct gem.", "block": 39, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/156c4d286b42ee7d8e879f5dd9d8525d466fb8f341eea299bf45bb2a005e43b2.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.68], [2, 0.68, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 1.16], [4, 1.16, 1.46], [5, 1.46, 2.02], [6, 2.02, 2.22], [8, 2.42, 2.7], [10, 3.18, 3.3], [11, 3.3, 3.44], [12, 3.44, 3.58], [13, 3.58, 3.7], [14, 3.7, 3.96], [15, 3.96, 4.22], [16, 4.22, 4.44], [17, 4.44, 4.82]]}, {"text": "gemsploit", "block": 40, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a7b7cca0dd6f78bc0f6859b9689b0b48b95b556b09ec558f4ef33b0cfd4b4544.mp3"}, {"text": "I wrote the gemsploit gem to explore what can happen with malicious code.", "block": 41, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8a908d5372ee532d76b822d44805a2a396434c7def459c4d56b86eae2c26c703.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.52], [4, 0.96, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.4], [6, 1.4, 1.8], [7, 1.8, 2.02], [8, 2.02, 2.16], [9, 2.16, 2.46], [10, 2.46, 2.7], [11, 2.7, 3.02], [12, 3.02, 3.44]]}, {"text": "By installing this gem, all of your ENV variables are posted up to jsonbin.org for public viewing.", "block": 42, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8d5333bf36285953292ef10cf20a3d1457de8effcb0acd9f6524423534ea626b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.52], [2, 0.52, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 1.02], [4, 1.56, 1.66], [5, 1.66, 1.84], [6, 1.84, 2.0], [7, 2.0, 2.44], [8, 2.44, 2.9], [9, 2.9, 3.16], [10, 3.16, 3.52], [11, 3.52, 3.76], [12, 3.76, 3.92], [14, 4.88, 5.12], [15, 5.12, 5.44], [16, 5.44, 5.78]]}, {"text": "My development machine had AWS secrets, bitcoin wallet secrets, and other hard-coded passwords.", "block": 42, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/84c2d1791bf7581bf83827b438001eddbc88db66c490f6c3a061a7e5fe27d7ff.mp3"}, {"text": "I have since moved to use dotenv to silo my env secret keys, but this still doesn’t protect gems from scanning your hard drive for unprotected BTC wallets.", "block": 42, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a207ee6fed6374917328903239cee7e3dcb4779f10e0404a6a8ee14ac9b80e76.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.38], [7, 1.78, 2.02], [8, 2.02, 2.4], [9, 2.4, 2.56], [11, 2.92, 3.24], [12, 3.24, 3.54], [13, 3.82, 4.36], [14, 4.36, 4.5], [15, 4.5, 4.7], [16, 4.7, 4.98], [17, 4.98, 5.2], [18, 5.2, 5.48], [19, 5.48, 5.76], [20, 5.76, 6.12], [21, 6.12, 6.34], [22, 6.34, 6.54], [23, 6.54, 6.72], [24, 6.72, 6.92], [25, 6.92, 7.42], [26, 7.42, 7.84], [27, 7.84, 8.36]]}, {"text": "Further Reading", "block": 43, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3865f6f8eb95a9a160e53d5a298eb6c728c58f396167c84261ddc086227e294c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.36, 0.84]]}, {"text": "[EN] How to take over a Ruby gem / Maciej Mensfeld @maciejmensfeld", "block": 44, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9eaa84e4ff52863184cac71cb1763cc93bc21b918bc3474c759481fff499be8b.mp3"}, {"text": "This conference talk was the inspiration for this exploration.", "block": 45, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8328320c72e6c8127cdcb9eb2fe5d41b4bb247470b5f252590e2aa92faa25dfb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.62], [2, 0.62, 0.92], [3, 0.92, 1.18], [4, 1.18, 1.38], [5, 1.38, 1.88], [6, 1.88, 2.18], [7, 2.18, 2.42], [8, 2.42, 3.02]]}, {"text": "Diffend", "block": 46, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3f8c0d18cdba89d71253feef25fae4fa4b84a4c9a9bfca7630797357e4cf2d96.mp3"}, {"text": "This is a really neat project that makes it easy to compare changes across versions of gems.", "block": 47, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2c159d5733279dfebae40e0ac14da8812bc9913de2e302432878f004713908a0.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.28], [2, 0.28, 0.38], [3, 0.38, 0.62], [4, 0.62, 0.82], [5, 0.82, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.66], [7, 1.66, 1.82], [8, 1.82, 2.02], [9, 2.02, 2.24], [10, 2.24, 2.42], [11, 2.42, 2.72], [12, 2.72, 3.22], [13, 3.22, 3.54], [14, 3.54, 4.0], [15, 4.0, 4.22], [16, 4.22, 4.46]]}, {"text": "You still have to take the time to audit the changes, but hopefully, with their clean interface, it does not take you too long.", "block": 47, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fd5b5c1c431ee1596e5b95e9e73b536b66bf1dea419bfd4bda7c7f58f2fbb64d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.1], [1, 0.1, 0.26], [2, 0.26, 0.44], [3, 0.44, 0.6], [4, 0.6, 0.74], [5, 0.74, 0.9], [6, 0.9, 1.12], [7, 1.12, 1.3], [8, 1.3, 1.54], [9, 1.54, 1.72], [10, 1.72, 2.12], [12, 2.44, 2.92], [13, 2.92, 3.48], [14, 3.48, 3.68], [15, 3.68, 3.94], [16, 3.94, 4.5], [17, 4.5, 4.96], [18, 4.96, 5.1], [19, 5.1, 5.28], [20, 5.28, 5.54], [21, 5.54, 5.72], [22, 5.72, 5.88], [23, 5.88, 6.16]]}, {"text": "Source Code", "block": 48, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7264c9c61afc737ae9106f3462b2ee0c3d8b6e4a99a837a6cbed659d00bb6592.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.32], [1, 0.32, 0.64]]}, {"text": "You can find the source code for lib-scanner on github.", "block": 49, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d419d61bcfd7c69e11aabbec7185887db8d61beb5f7b3abf827f115886e2e62c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.52], [3, 0.52, 0.66], [4, 0.66, 0.86], [5, 0.86, 1.12], [6, 1.12, 1.32], [8, 1.84, 2.04], [9, 2.04, 2.22]]}, {"text": "The project is (mostly) written in golang with an in-depth readme file explaining how the code pipeline works.", "block": 49, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/083bcdec9cedad8eeded5781a26dd252b53b773a49bd201ebc2e0fc39ed28921.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.12], [1, 0.12, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.92], [3, 0.98, 1.54], [4, 2.0, 2.22], [5, 2.22, 2.4], [7, 2.74, 2.92], [8, 2.92, 3.06], [10, 3.48, 3.82], [11, 3.82, 4.08], [12, 4.08, 4.54], [13, 4.54, 4.78], [14, 4.78, 4.9], [15, 4.9, 5.08], [16, 5.08, 5.4], [17, 5.4, 5.76]]}, {"text": "Future work", "block": 50, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ab5eabe7bc3dc65d57601ba1582063f96ef1017a3344c202bdf48b3adc63bf48.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.46], [1, 0.46, 0.86]]}, {"text": "I’d love to bring this scanner to other languages like golang or python.", "block": 51, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7de27c2530bdfbb6d90cb3fff46b3f5841daf555f5d9e9071e624fdfbdf68689.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.34], [1, 0.34, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.86], [5, 1.02, 1.38], [6, 1.38, 1.58], [7, 1.58, 1.78], [8, 1.78, 2.12], [9, 2.12, 2.5], [11, 2.92, 3.22], [12, 3.22, 3.56]]}, {"text": "Please shoot me an email (kevin at sparkstart.io) if you’re interested in collaborating!", "block": 51, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fd2de250685c3c52b2baeab5f212c9551bf5717e01e3f00529d80037157e6f49.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.5], [2, 0.5, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.76], [4, 0.76, 1.08], [5, 1.4, 1.6], [6, 1.6, 1.74], [8, 2.54, 2.86], [9, 2.86, 3.02], [10, 3.02, 3.34], [11, 3.34, 3.5], [12, 3.5, 3.88]]}]}